{
  "tema": 6862,
  "slug": "este-ese-aquel-distancia",
  "titulo": "This, that, that over there: este, ese, aquel",
  "subtitulo": "«Esta llave, ese desarmador, aquel barco.»",
  "foto": "t02.jpg",
  "regla": "Spanish has three distances: este (this, near me), ese (that, near you or a little away) and aquel (that over there, far from both of us). All three go before the noun and agree with it in gender and number.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": null,
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**este** = _this_: near the speaker (**aquí**)."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**ese** = _that_: near the listener, or a little away (**ahí**)."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**aquel** = _that (over there)_: far from both people (**allá**)."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "",
            "masc. sing.",
            "fem. sing.",
            "masc. pl.",
            "fem. pl."
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "near me",
              "este",
              "esta",
              "estos",
              "estas"
            ],
            [
              "near you",
              "ese",
              "esa",
              "esos",
              "esas"
            ],
            [
              "far from both",
              "aquel",
              "aquella",
              "aquellos",
              "aquellas"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "They agree with the noun: **esta** llave, **esos** carros, **aquellas** olas."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Distance in time works the same way: **este** año (now), **ese** día (one we just mentioned), **aquella** época (long ago)."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "In everyday Mexican speech **ese** often covers anything not near you; **aquel** stresses that it's really far."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "==Esta== llave abre la puerta de la casa.",
              "en": "This key opens the front door."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿Me pasas ==ese== desarmador que tienes ahí?",
              "en": "Can you pass me that screwdriver you've got there?"
            },
            {
              "es": "¿Ves ==aquellas== olas allá, cerca de las rocas?",
              "en": "See those waves over there, near the rocks?"
            },
            {
              "es": "==Estos== jitomates son de mi huerto.",
              "en": "These tomatoes are from my garden."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Esa== camiseta que traes está padrísima.",
              "en": "That T-shirt you're wearing is awesome."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Aquel== edificio del fondo es el hospital.",
              "en": "That building at the back is the hospital."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿Te acuerdas de ==aquel== verano en Ensenada?",
              "en": "Do you remember that summer in Ensenada?"
            },
            {
              "es": "==Este== fin de semana tengo torneo de jiu-jitsu.",
              "en": "This weekend I have a jiu-jitsu tournament."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
